The Konomi SLM

Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by Thomas Frumkin.

Draws on three of Gary W. Floyd's Guided Entropy Principle (GEP) papers. The Konomi SLM
itself is the estate's own work.
  - Keeping a rule only if it predicts held-out data (so a confident but wrong prior
    cannot take hold) and allowing "I don't know" as an answer:
    Gary W. Floyd, Lumiea Systems Research Division — ThunderStruck Service LLC — "From GEP Stabilization to Dual-Map Ethical Reasoning: A derivation of positive ethical evidence, negative ethical evidence, and non-legal moral reasoning," Derivation v0.2. Open Defensive Prior Art (Creative Commons).
  - The sleep cycle (consolidate at night, keep a dream only if it passes a check):
    Gary W. Floyd, Lumiea Systems Research Division — ThunderStruck Service LLC — "Dream State Architecture: GEP-Guided Memory Consolidation and Entropy Regulation in Artificial Consciousness Systems," 2025. Open Defensive Prior Art (Creative Commons).
  - Knowledge living outside the model, with the model only proposing and routing:
    Gary W. Floyd, Lumiea Systems Research Division — ThunderStruck Service LLC — "NEXUS — Distributed Synthetic Intelligence: Architecture, Ethics, and the GEP-Native Mind," 2026. Open Defensive Prior Art (Creative Commons).

Vendored under ./vendor/seed-library (verbatim), reused and credited:
  - the grow -> grade-on-held-out ribosome, seeded RNG, stratified split and AUC
    (seed-library / fall-spore / pattern-organs, sjgant80-hub)
  - the SENTINEL-style verify-before-you-parse guard
  - the hand-rolled FIPS-180-4 SHA-256 / HMAC

Real data: Online Shoppers Purchasing Intention dataset — Sakar & Kastro,
UCI Machine Learning Repository (2018), DOI 10.24432/C5F88Q, CC BY 4.0.
The three survival domains (triage, water, crop) are realistic-synthetic,
generated deterministically from a known rule plus seeded noise — stated on
the page and in domains.mjs.
